    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="contextory-v0-4-0" tabindex="-1">Contextory v0.4.0 <a class="header-anchor" href="#contextory-v0-4-0" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Contextory v0.4.0&quot;">\u200B</a></h1><p>Map other local codebases alongside your current application. Reference repositories help developers and agents understand an existing architecture, investigate migration sources and learn implementation patterns while keeping the active project&#39;s source graph and work records separate.</p><h2 id="changes" tabindex="-1">Changes <a class="header-anchor" href="#changes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Changes&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><ul><li>Use <strong>Architecture \u2192 Add reference</strong> to register up to eight local codebases. Choose a repository in <strong>Codebase</strong> to explore its subsystem map, entry points, symbols and connections. The sidebar and Architecture workbench keep independent selections for side-by-side exploration.</li><li>Keep each reference in a separate persistent source index and analysis worker. Registrations survive restarts; queries for different repositories can run concurrently. Analysis writes no source, configuration, requirements or checks into the reference.</li><li>Give agents <code>contextory_codebase_list</code> and <code>contextory_codebase_change</code>, plus explicit <code>codebaseId</code> selection on architecture, context, search, impact, path, index/import and flow trace/expand tools. Omitted or <code>current</code> always selects the active project. Responses identify the reference root so same-path symbols remain distinguishable.</li><li>Add CLI <code>references</code>, <code>reference-add</code>, <code>reference-remove</code> and source-command <code>--codebase</code> selection. Update portable skills and shared native/headless guidance with reference scope, freshness and citation rules.</li><li>Scope source navigation and flow tracing to the selected repository, reject responses from previous selections, and keep current-project unsaved editor buffers out of reference analysis. <strong>Detach reference</strong> leaves its source untouched and retains rebuildable cached projections under the owning service storage.</li><li>Support long Windows editor-storage paths when opening SQLite ledgers and reference projections.</li></ul><p>Understanding a reference does not automatically apply its design, change requirements or migrate code. Ask the agent explicitly when you want to implement something in the current application. See the <a href="./../CODEBASE-INTELLIGENCE.html#analyze-reference-codebases">reference-codebase guide</a> for agent and CLI examples.</p><h2 id="install-or-upgrade" tabindex="-1">Install or upgrade <a class="header-anchor" href="#install-or-upgrade" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Install or upgrade&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><ol><li>Use Windows, Node.js <strong>24+</strong>, and VS Code <strong>1.96+</strong> or IBM Bob with one trusted local project folder.</li><li>Download <code>contextory-workspace-0.4.0.vsix</code> and <code>contextory-workspace-0.4.0.sha256</code> from the <a href="https://github.com/igormicadei/Contextory/releases/tag/v0.4.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub release</a>. Compare the package SHA-256 with the checksum file.</li><li>Choose <strong>Extensions \u2192 \u2026 \u2192 Install from VSIX\u2026</strong>, select the package and reload the editor. VS Code users can run <code>code --install-extension .\\contextory-workspace-0.4.0.vsix</code>.</li><li>Reload existing native MCP connections or restart their sessions to discover the updated tool catalog. Native agents keep their own permissions and authentication.</li></ol><p>Existing schema 4 project records remain compatible. References are registered in the owning workspace service and indexed under its storage; no separate editor workspace or companion installation is needed in the reference. Keep using the same storage or editor descriptor with the standalone CLI. Python 3.10+ is needed for Python analysis.</p><h2 id="validation-and-limits" tabindex="-1">Validation and limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#validation-and-limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Validation and limits&quot;">\u200B</a></h2><p>Validation includes <strong>63 backend tests</strong>, <strong>29 UI tests</strong>, typechecking, canonical/workspace skill checks and a complete <strong>23-page</strong> documentation build. Extracted-package scenarios pass in VS Code <strong>1.145.3</strong> and IBM Bob, VS Code API <strong>1.126.0</strong>, including same-path unsaved-buffer isolation and unchanged reference source after detachment. See the <a href="./../VALIDATION.html">validation record</a>.</p><p>References refresh saved files on demand; cached architecture is explicit. Reference search uses lexical graph matching, with a reported lexical fallback for hybrid mode. Existing TS/JS, Python and optional Graphify coverage limits apply independently to each repository. Static relationships describe possible connections, not observed execution or test coverage. Remote cloning, automatic cross-repository graph edges/migration, authenticated-model conversations, other operating systems and large-repository performance are not qualified by this release.</p><p>Browse the <a href="https://igormicadei.github.io/Contextory/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">complete documentation</a> for user guides, tools and portable skills. Distribution uses GitHub release assets. The project remains <strong>UNLICENSED</strong>.</p>', 12)
